+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XdY1PLh29zjBNrD7wy4NZP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n2\t\n3\tImplement a `TaskQueue` class with the following interface:\n4\t\n5\t## Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`enqueue(payload)`** - Add a task to the queue. Returns the created task object.\n8\t- **`dequeue()`** - Remove and return the next task in FIFO order. Returns `null` if the queue is empty. Sets the task status to `processing`.\n9\t- **`size()`** - Return the number of pending tasks in the queue.\n10\t\n11\t## Task Object\n12\t\n13\tEach task has the following properties:\n14\t\n15\t| Property    | Type     | Description                                    |\n16\t|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|\n17\t| `id`        | `string` | Auto-generated unique identifier (UUID format) |\n18\t| `payload`   | `any`    | The data associated with the task              |\n19\t| `status`    | `string` | One of: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n20\t| `createdAt` | `Date`   | Timestamp when the task was created            |\n21\t\n22\t## Requirements\n23\t\n24\t- Tasks are returned in the order they were added (First-In, First-Out)\n25\t- Each task gets a unique `id` automatically assigned\n26\t- New tasks start with `status: 'pending'`\n27\t- When dequeued, task status changes to `'processing'`\n28\t- `dequeue()` returns `null` when the queue is empty\n29\t\n30\t## Export\n31\t\n32\tExport the `TaskQueue` class as a named export from `src/index.ts`.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"61321d1d-2cc2-4e38-b507-aa91a5fe8630","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:48.244Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
