+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZevti9UXmNaxTua9KLidu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 2: Named Queues\n2\t\n3\tExtend the `TaskQueue` to support multiple named queues.\n4\t\n5\t## Updated Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`enqueue(queueName, payload)`** - Add a task to a specific named queue. Returns the created task.\n8\t- **`dequeue(queueName)`** - Get the next task from a specific named queue. Returns `null` if queue is empty or doesn't exist.\n9\t- **`listQueues()`** - Return an array of all queue names that have been created.\n10\t- **`queueSize(queueName)`** - Return the number of pending tasks in a specific queue.\n11\t\n12\t## Requirements\n13\t\n14\t- Each named queue operates independently\n15\t- Enqueueing to a queue that doesn't exist creates it\n16\t- Dequeueing from a non-existent queue returns `null`\n17\t- If no queue name is specified, use `'default'` as the queue name\n18\t- `listQueues()` returns names of all queues that have been created\n19\t- Queue-specific sizes are tracked independently\n20\t\n21\t## Backward Compatibility\n22\t\n23\tThe single-argument `enqueue(payload)` should still work by using the `'default'` queue.\n24\tSimilarly, `dequeue()` with no arguments should dequeue from `'default'`.\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"f663ab6d-f4e4-4126-96ed-df4dda5278f4","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:48.466Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
