+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0124p43TrbkimhgRGSJJTmrB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 4: Delayed/Scheduled Tasks\n2\t\n3\tAdd support for delayed and scheduled task execution.\n4\t\n5\t## Updated Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n8\t  - `delay`: number of milliseconds before the task becomes available\n9\t  - `runAt`: a `Date` object specifying when the task should become available\n10\t  - (existing) `priority`: priority level\n11\t\n12\t## Requirements\n13\t\n14\t- A delayed task is enqueued immediately but not returned by `dequeue()` until the delay has elapsed\n15\t- A `runAt` task becomes available at the specified time\n16\t- Non-delayed tasks should be dequeued before delayed tasks that haven't become available yet\n17\t- When multiple delayed tasks are available, they are ordered by their availability time (earliest first), then by priority, then FIFO\n18\t- `delay` and `runAt` work with named queues\n19\t- The task object should include a `availableAt` property (Date) indicating when the task becomes available\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"54f65d45-183b-4791-acc0-7f7bcee6c675","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:48.885Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KmMbjriq4y67CMYzP6Lnjh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n2\t\n3\tAdd automatic retry functionality with exponential backoff.\n4\t\n5\t## New Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`fail(taskId, error?)`** - Mark a processing task as failed. Triggers automatic retry if retries remain.\n8\t- **`complete(taskId)`** - Mark a processing task as completed.\n9\t\n10\t## Updated Methods\n11\t\n12\t- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n13\t  - `maxRetries`: maximum number of retry attempts (default: 3)\n14\t  - `backoffMs`: base delay for exponential backoff in milliseconds (default: 1000)\n15\t\n16\t## Requirements\n17\t\n18\t- When `fail()` is called and retries remain, the task is re-enqueued with a delay\n19\t- Backoff formula: `backoffMs * 2^(attempt - 1)` where attempt starts at 1\n20\t  - 1st retry: 1000ms, 2nd retry: 2000ms, 3rd retry: 4000ms\n21\t- `task.attempts` tracks how many times the task has been attempted (starts at 1 on first dequeue)\n22\t- Custom `maxRetries` can be set per task\n23\t- Retried tasks preserve their original queue name and priority\n24\t- If a task has exhausted all retries, it remains in `failed` status (see Phase 6 for DLQ)\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"1a359367-0611-478c-8407-499777fff0ca","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:48.885Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
