+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0191dGCsj56jF342gvHa5qXi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 6: Dead Letter Queue\n2\t\n3\tAdd dead letter queue (DLQ) support for tasks that have exhausted all retries.\n4\t\n5\t## New Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`getDLQ(queueName)`** - Return an array of all dead-letter tasks for the specified queue.\n8\t- **`retryDLQ(taskId)`** - Move a dead-letter task back to its original queue for another round of retries. Returns the re-enqueued task.\n9\t- **`clearDLQ(queueName)`** - Remove all dead-letter tasks for the specified queue.\n10\t\n11\t## Requirements\n12\t\n13\t- When a task exhausts all retry attempts (from Phase 5), it automatically moves to the DLQ\n14\t- DLQ tasks have status `'failed'` and are stored separately from the main queue\n15\t- Each DLQ task retains its original error information (`task.lastError`)\n16\t- DLQ tasks track how many times they've failed (`task.failCount`)\n17\t- `retryDLQ(taskId)` resets the task's retry count, giving it a fresh set of retries\n18\t- `retryDLQ(taskId)` places the task back in its original queue with original priority\n19\t- `clearDLQ(queueName)` removes all DLQ entries for that queue\n20\t- DLQ is per-queue (each named queue has its own DLQ)\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"f93a38eb-7554-4178-a17b-7bc1ddfa7878","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:49.005Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
