+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5PQznAheYuXjhg9imi4qN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 7: Task Dependencies\n2\t\n3\tAdd support for task dependencies, where tasks can wait for other tasks to complete before becoming available.\n4\t\n5\t## Updated Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n8\t  - `dependsOn`: an array of task IDs that must complete before this task becomes available\n9\t\n10\t## New Methods\n11\t\n12\t- **`getDependencies(taskId)`** - Return dependency information for a task, including each dependency's ID and current status.\n13\t\n14\t## Requirements\n15\t\n16\t- A task with dependencies remains blocked (not available for dequeue) until ALL dependencies have `completed` status\n17\t- When a dependency completes (via `complete(taskId)`), the system checks if any dependent tasks are now unblocked\n18\t- Circular dependencies must be detected and throw an error at enqueue time\n19\t  - Direct circular: A depends on B, B depends on A\n20\t  - Indirect circular: A → B → C → A\n21\t- `getDependencies(taskId)` returns an array of `{ taskId, status }` objects\n22\t- Dependency on a non-existent task ID should throw an error\n23\t- A failed dependency does NOT auto-fail the dependent task - it stays blocked\n24\t- Cascading dependencies work: if A depends on B and B depends on C, A is only available after both B and C complete\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"dd89196d-b6bc-4d4a-8820-45a4f2a0e3fb","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:50.360Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
