+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MQcVcNuQHj2rcMCfaprdym","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 8: Concurrency Control\n2\t\n3\tAdd per-queue concurrency limits to control how many tasks can be processed simultaneously.\n4\t\n5\t## New Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`setConcurrency(queueName, limit)`** - Set the maximum number of tasks that can be in `processing` status simultaneously for a queue.\n8\t- **`getConcurrency(queueName)`** - Return concurrency information: `{ current: number, max: number }`.\n9\t\n10\t## Requirements\n11\t\n12\t- `dequeue()` returns `null` if the queue has reached its concurrency limit, even if tasks are available\n13\t- `complete(taskId)` and `fail(taskId)` free up a concurrency slot\n14\t- Default concurrency is unlimited (no limit) until `setConcurrency` is called\n15\t- Each queue has its own independent concurrency limit\n16\t- Concurrency interacts correctly with priorities (highest priority task still chosen, but only if a slot is available)\n17\t- `getConcurrency(queueName)` returns the current number of processing tasks and the configured maximum\n18\t  - For unlimited queues, `max` should be `Infinity` or `0` to indicate no limit\n19\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"6a02e5db-03bf-411b-971f-af5eab435b5c","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:50.587Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
