+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qbud1AaqTD1eWpm5XhTBjh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 9: Progress and Cancellation\n2\t\n3\tAdd progress tracking and task cancellation support.\n4\t\n5\t## New Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`updateProgress(taskId, percent, message?)`** - Report progress for a processing task (0-100).\n8\t- **`getProgress(taskId)`** - Return progress info: `{ percent: number, message?: string, updatedAt: Date }`.\n9\t- **`cancel(taskId)`** - Cancel a pending or processing task. Sets status to `'cancelled'`.\n10\t- **`onProgress(taskId, callback)`** - Subscribe to progress updates. Callback receives `{ percent, message, updatedAt }`.\n11\t\n12\t## Requirements\n13\t\n14\t- Progress percentage must be between 0 and 100\n15\t- `updateProgress` fires all registered `onProgress` callbacks for that task\n16\t- `cancel()` works on both `pending` and `processing` tasks\n17\t- A cancelled pending task is removed from the queue (not available for dequeue)\n18\t- A cancelled processing task has its status set to `'cancelled'`\n19\t- Cancelled tasks are NOT retried (even if they have retries remaining)\n20\t- `getProgress(taskId)` returns `null` if no progress has been reported yet\n21\t- The `message` parameter in `updateProgress` is optional\n22\t- `onProgress` returns an unsubscribe function\n23\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"9d89f051-425c-4b97-88df-4bd95668128a","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:50.800Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
