+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qz9eukk6qpqsYh7mUqDnd6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 12: Graceful Shutdown\n2\t\n3\tAdd graceful shutdown capabilities to the task queue.\n4\t\n5\t## New Methods\n6\t\n7\t- **`shutdown(timeout?)`** - Initiate graceful shutdown. Returns a Promise that resolves with a summary.\n8\t  - `timeout`: maximum milliseconds to wait for processing tasks (default: 30000)\n9\t- **`onShutdown(callback)`** - Register a callback to be called during shutdown.\n10\t\n11\t## Requirements\n12\t\n13\t- After `shutdown()` is called, `enqueue()` should throw an error\n14\t- `shutdown()` waits for all currently processing tasks to complete\n15\t- If processing tasks don't complete within the timeout, they are force-cancelled\n16\t- `onShutdown` callbacks are called during the shutdown process\n17\t- The returned summary object includes:\n18\t  - `completed`: number of tasks that completed during shutdown\n19\t  - `cancelled`: number of tasks that were force-cancelled\n20\t  - `elapsed`: time in milliseconds the shutdown took\n21\t- Multiple calls to `shutdown()` should be idempotent (return the same promise/result)\n22\t- If there are no processing tasks, shutdown resolves immediately\n23\t- Force-cancelled tasks have their status set to `'cancelled'`\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RHRBicVF9uaSx2wJ5fEg5h","session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"9d29d7fb-2f85-4d9b-83ad-6bc7636d35a6","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:58:51.146Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore project structure"}
