rue,\n    \"declarationMap\": true,\n    \"sourceMap\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\", \"dist\", \"tests\"]\n}\n```\n\n**vitest.config.ts** (Full Content):\n```typescript\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  test: {\n    globals: true,\n    testTimeout: 10000,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### src/index.ts\n**Status**: File does not exist yet. This is where you need to implement the `TaskQueue` class.\n\n---\n\n## 12-Phase Specification Summary\n\n### Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n- **Methods**: `enqueue(queueName, payload)`, `dequeue(queueName)`, `size()`\n- **Task properties**: `id` (UUID), `payload`, `status` (pending/processing/completed/failed), `createdAt`\n- Default queue name: `'default'`\n- Tasks dequeue in FIFO order\n\n### Phase 2: Named Queues\n- **New Methods**: `listQueues()`, `queueSize(queueName)`\n- Multiple independent named queues\n- Default queue name when not specified\n- Each queue operates independently\n\n### Phase 3: Priority\n- **Option**: `priority` (1-10, default 5, lower = higher priority)\n- Dequeue by highest priority first (lowest number)\n- FIFO within same priority level\n- Throws on priority outside 1-10 range\n\n### Phase 4: Delayed/Scheduled Tasks\n- **Options**: `delay` (ms), `runAt` (Date)\n- Task unavailable until delay/runAt time expires\n- Task property: `availableAt` (Date)\n- Non-delayed tasks dequeue before delayed ones\n- Multiple delayed tasks ordered by availability time → priority → FIFO\n\n### Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n- **New Methods**: `fail(taskId, error?)`, `complete(taskId)`\n- **Options**: `maxRetries` (default 3), `backoffMs` (default 1000)\n- Backoff formula: `backoffMs * 2^(attempt - 1)`\n- Task property: `attempts` (incremented on each dequeue)\n- Failed task re-enqueued with delay if retries remain\n- Preserves original queue, priority, and other properties\n\n### Phase 6: Dead Letter Queue (DLQ)\n- **New Methods**: `getDLQ(queueName)`, `retryDLQ(taskId)`, `clearDLQ(queueName)`\n- Task moves to DLQ after exhausting all retries\n- DLQ properties: `lastError`, `failCount`\n- `retryDLQ()` resets retry count and puts task back in original queue\n- DLQ is per-queue\n\n### Phase 7: Task Dependencies\n- **Option**: `dependsOn` (array of task IDs)\n- **New Method**: `getDependencies(taskId)` returns `[{ taskId, status }, ...]`\n- Task unavailable until all dependencies have `completed` status\n- Circular dependency detection (throws error)\n- Failed dependency doesn't auto-fail dependent\n- Cascading dependencies supported\n\n### Phase 8: Concurrency Control\n- **New Methods**: `setConcurrency(queueName, limit)`, `getConcurrency(queueName)` → `{ current, max }`\n- Default: unlimited (no limit)\n- `dequeue()` returns null if at limit\n- `complete()` and `fail()` free a slot\n- Per-queue limits, independent from each other\n- Still respects priority when slot is available\n\n### Phase 9: Progress and Cancellation\n- **New Methods**: `updateProgress(taskId, percent, message?)`, `getProgress(taskId)` → `{ percent, message?, updatedAt }`, `cancel(taskId)`, `onProgress(taskId, callback)` → unsubscribe function\n- Progress: 0-100 range\n- `cancel()` removes pending tasks from queue\n- `cancel()` sets status to `'cancelled'` for processing tasks\n- Cancelled tasks are NOT retried\n- `onProgress` fires all callbacks registered for task\n- `getProgress` returns null if no progress reported\n\n### Phase 10: Recurring Tasks (Cron)\n- **New Methods**: `schedule(queueName, cronExpression, taskTemplate)`, `unschedule(scheduleId)`, `listSchedules(queueName?)`, `tick()`\n- **Cron subset**: `*/N * * * *` (every N minutes), `0 * * * *` (every hour), `0 0 * * *` (every day)\n- Returns schedule object: `{ id, queueName, cronExpression, taskTemplate, active: true }`\n- `tick()` checks and enqueues due tasks (manual trigger for testing)\n- Multiple schedules can coexist\n\n### Phase 11: Middleware Pipeline\n- **New Methods**: `use(queueName, middleware)`, `process(queueName, handler)`\n- **Middleware signature**: `(task, next) => Promise<void>`\n- Middlewares run in order added (first added = first to run)\n- Each middleware must call `next()` or processing skips\n- Middleware can modify task object\n- Error in middleware marks task as failed\n- Independent middleware stacks per queue\n\n### Phase 12: Graceful Shutdown\n- **New Methods**: `shutdown(timeout?)` → Promise with summary, `onShutdown(callback)`\n- `shutdown()` prevents new `enqueue()` calls (throws error)\n- Waits for all processing tasks to complete\n- Force-cancels tasks after timeout (default 30000ms)\n- Returns summary: `{ completed: number, cancelled: number, elapsed: number }`\n- Multiple calls are idempotent (return same result)\n- `onShutdown` callbacks fired during shutdown\n\n---\n\n## Test Files Summary\n\nAll 90 tests (across 12 files) validate:\n\n- **phase-01.test.ts**: 8 tests - Basic FIFO functionality, task properties, uniqueness\n- **phase-02.test.ts**: 8 tests - Named queues independence, listQueues, queueSize\n- **phase-03.test.ts**: 9 tests - Priority ordering, FIFO within priority, validation\n- **phase-04.test.ts**: 7 tests - Delayed tasks, runAt scheduling, availability timing\n- **phase-05.test.ts**: 8 tests - Retry mechanics, exponential backoff, maxRetries, preservation\n- **phase-06.test.ts**: 8 tests - DLQ functionality, retryDLQ, clearDLQ, error/fail tracking\n- **phase-07.test.ts**: 8 tests - Dependencies, circular detection, cascading, getDependencies\n- **phase-08.test.ts**: 7 tests - Concurrency limits, slot management, per-queue independence\n- **phase-09.test.ts**: 8 tests - Progress tracking, cancellation, callbacks, optional message\n- **phase-10.test.ts**: 7 tests - Cron scheduling, tick(), multiple schedules, queue placement\n- **phase-11.test.ts**: 8 tests - Middleware pipeline, error handling, task modification, per-queue stacks\n- **phase-12.test.ts**: 8 tests - Graceful shutdown, timeout, callbacks, idempotence\n\n---\n\n## Critical Implementation Notes\n\n1. **No external runtime dependencies** - only dev dependencies provided\n2. **Tests use `vi.useFakeTimers()`** - timing-sensitive tests use Vitest's fake timers\n3. **UUID generation** - tasks need unique string IDs\n4. **All in one file** - implementation must be in `src/index.ts`\n5. **TypeScript strict mode** - `strict: true` in tsconfig\n6. **ES2022 target** - modern JavaScript features available\n7. **Tests import as**: `import { TaskQueue } from '../src/index.js'` (named export)\n\nThe project is a comprehensive task queue system test harness with 12 progressively complex phases, testing everything from basic FIFO queuing to advanced features like middleware pipelines and graceful shutdown."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f122924-a0ea-4945-8ed2-52b5e52c9c41","uuid":"491d7d02-dfb4-4df3-848d-a8020eda0210","timestamp":"2026-06-30T20:59:17.994Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the project at /workspace. I need to understand:\n1. The directory structure (especially src/, phases/, and any config files)\n2. The content of src/index.ts (starter file)\n3. The content of all files in phases/ directory\n4. package.json and tsconfig.json\n5. Any test files\n\nPlease read all these files completely and return their full contents. This is critical for implementing a TaskQueue class.","agentId":"a9a7487fd6dc4d053","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information you need. Let me compile a comprehensive report:\n\n---\n\n## Project Exploration Report\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── src/                          # Source code (currently empty)\n├── phases/                       # 12 phase specifications (phase-01.md through phase-12.md)\n├── tests/                        # 12 test files (one per phase)\n├── .git/                         # Git repository\n├── package.json                